PHASE A CODE PATCH DRAFT (companion to Migration 027 — applied 2026-05-29).

Scope:
  Part 1 — Write-through patches across 7 existing files (~75 LOC). Keeps
           existing tp1/tp2 behavior intact; in parallel populates new `tp`
           column with the SAME value as tp1. Reads use COALESCE(tp, tp1).
           No functional change to trade entry/exit logic in this phase.
  Part 2 — 3 NEW pattern/ module files: __init__.py, clusterer.py, registry.py.
  Part 3 — 1 NEW pretrainer file: pattern_cluster_train.py.

NOT in this draft (deferred to later phases):
  - Single-TP 100% close behavior (Phase C — gated on predictor existing)
  - celery_app.py new beat tasks `update_pattern_registry` + `cleanup_stale_predictions`
  - dashboard/api.py UI surfacing of tp column / pattern cluster
  - prediction/refresh_loop.py + prediction/xgb_predictor.py (Phase B)

================================================================================
PART 1 — WRITE-THROUGH PATCHES (7 files, ~75 LOC)
================================================================================

The principle: every site that writes tp1 also writes tp (same value). Every
site that reads tp1 from Redis uses COALESCE(tp, tp1) (or the Python equivalent
for Redis reads). This is reversible (revert to ignoring tp; functional state
unchanged) and lets the new `tp` column accumulate consistent data.

